  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "ea7cbbe900d9a65558b888d6b6afbee251ae0a17",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1275887667,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I think we should add a new `WIRESHARK_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE` above called \"win64arm\" or whatever, and then set processor architecture from that.\n\n```cmake\n\telseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES \"aarch64|ARM64\")\n\t\tset(WIRESHARK_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE win64arm)\n```\n\nthen later\n\n```cmake\n\telseif(WIRESHARK_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE MATCHES \"win64arm\")\n\t\tset(WIRESHARK_TARGET_PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE arm64)\n```\n\n@Biswa96 what do you think?",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-02-13T09:25:16.455Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-02-13T09:25:16.455Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 205044318,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 9794,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "187bde9bc73502356039d353dd60c8c333699042",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1275979638,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I have only used msys2 to compile Wireshark for AArch64 architecture. So, the `set(WIRESHARK_TARGET_PLATFORM \"$ENV{MSYSTEM_CARCH}\")` line takes care of it. Adding that `set(WIRESHARK_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE win64arm)` would also mean Visual Studio can compile Wireshark for AArch64. I did not test the build in MSVC. Feel free to add if it compiles in your case.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6402851,
            "username": "Biswa96",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Biswapriyo Nath",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6402851/avatar.png?v=1788961788",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/Biswa96"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-02-13T10:16:29.649Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-02-13T10:16:29.649Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 205044318,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 9794,
